  "criterion_identities": {
    "version": "acceptance-coverage-criterion-identity.v1",
    "identities": [
      {
        "position": 0,
        "text": "PURPOSE. Add one shared server-side semantic skeleton composer consumed by the existing WK-2419 obligation-source describe and WK-2417 acceptance-mapping describe operations, so an agent starts from authenticated current criteria, contract nodes, admitted pack components and mutation arguments instead of manually reconstructing rows. Do not add a preparation route or another public authoring bootstrap.",
        "identity": "derived:13befeb806b1453ddb33743bf0d4eb20840d7a44796ab8028fd292e9c9f784ca",
        "source": "derived"
      },
      {
        "position": 1,
        "text": "SEMANTIC AUTHORITY STAYS WITH THE CALLER. A skeleton may enumerate current identities, allowed typed alternatives, required authored fields and unresolved slots; it must not invent an obligation statement, choose a mechanism, claim proof adequacy, select a gap disposition, assign coverage axes, or confer lifecycle authority.",
        "identity": "derived:cc2300d3e41aa10f7bc47784d742fdc98bfea8269fa79b9a765e651c2aad8ea0",
        "source": "derived"
      },
      {
        "position": 2,
        "text": "CLOSED 39-ENTRY VOCABULARY. The controlled contract's ordered ref-skeleton-entry-01 through ref-skeleton-entry-39 population is exhaustive. It fixes common server/evolving/projection/transport/metric entries, nine obligation-row and mutation entries, and three acceptance-row entries. Implementations consume those stable identities and their encoded server-versus-authored categories and type alternatives; workers do not create, remove, merge, reorder or reinterpret an entry.",
        "identity": "derived:cb07a2fbe934731e5a7655d41cdf6646897925cc079b08afb46e13ede4dc53b9",
        "source": "derived"
      },
      {
        "position": 3,
        "text": "SERVER COMPOSITION. The shared composer receives only server-resolved WK/unit/focus, criteria, controlled-contract nodes, proof plan/selected pack, source/carrier state, bounds and existing create/upsert identities from the owning describe operations. Public schemas accept no paths, raw carriers, caller pack identities, canonical digests beyond mutation CAS inputs, or authority claims.",
        "identity": "derived:e30a884d5130db10d4a59fd552db45dd99e463f4507d7380a96791399b488712",
        "source": "derived"
      },
      {
        "position": 4,
        "text": "LOSSLESS BOUNDED PROJECTION. The complete deterministic 39-entry population remains available through the server/MCP transport boundary. Each existing describe operation exposes an inline gap-first skeleton projection of at most 16,384 canonical UTF-8 bytes with exact total/returned/omitted counts; when omitted is nonzero, the existing integrity-bound content-reference transport binds the complete population so all 39 identities are reconstructible. WK-2439 defines no parallel cursor, continuation, state machine, route, spill format or repeat-describe recovery.",
        "identity": "derived:76db427b3e09405b868f580237161a13918f22182d474914d8198030f857ddda",
        "source": "derived"
      },
      {
        "position": 5,
        "text": "EXECUTABLE HANDOFF. For absent carriers, completed authored decisions compose directly into the existing WK-2419 or WK-2417 create request. For current carriers, stable tool identity and non-CAS fixed arguments are emitted once, while expected_content_digest and every digest-bearing carrier identity are evolving state owned by existing mutation receipts: each single-row call consumes the prior receipt digest, emits the next, and final query/describe verifies the complete carrier. WK-2438 batch is used only when canonically available.",
        "identity": "derived:e4fb5a26a3570156aaa417d368a288a1f5f33a57d5fbf0b7248d54a3821acd2c",
        "source": "derived"
      },
      {
        "position": 6,
        "text": "FRESH-SESSION COMPLETENESS. A restarted orchestrator discovers and calls the existing obligation or acceptance describe operation, fills only the semantic decisions exposed by its skeleton projection, submits through the advertised existing mutations with receipt-fed CAS state, reconstructs any omitted entries through the existing content reference, and verifies canonical final state without source inspection, raw JSON editing or hidden retained context.",
        "identity": "derived:107d0639050f43b44a5f37f0e2ccbab42ba4f85b39ac3f47db26785fbfcedb60",
        "source": "derived"
      },
      {
        "position": 7,
        "text": "LOCAL FAILURE DATA ONLY. The composer deterministically reports missing local inputs, invalid authored decisions, unresolved slots and bound overflow to the owning describe operation. WK-2437 exclusively owns public state classification, recovery-call selection, next_calls, blind-retry prevention and dependency recovery; WK-2439 must not synthesize an independent recovery workflow.",
        "identity": "derived:24144c151b44aaec531a976b1991007329e6fa143d67ed270fabac3492da54ae",
        "source": "derived"
      },
      {
        "position": 8,
        "text": "MEASUREMENT HANDOFF. The existing MCP fresh-session proof captures fixed-fixture raw call count, request/result UTF-8 bytes, unresolved-slot count, retry count, source-inspection-escape count and exact final-carrier-equivalence boolean, and compares the persisted carrier byte-for-byte with the intended complete authored state. WK-2055 exclusively owns composed-versus-manual reporting, denominators, conclusions and publication of conformance claims.",
        "identity": "derived:bae3c9de7f38f45cad872d009020922ac227a896ff6314e49322757fd01c1a7c",
        "source": "derived"
      },
      {
        "position": 9,
        "text": "ROLE AND AUTHORITY. Skeleton composition is read-only and non-authoritative; writes occur only through the existing authenticated WK-2417/WK-2419 mutation operations. Role visibility remains that of the owning describe operation and never widens mutation permissions.",
        "identity": "derived:d8168a23d25effd48985cb7488fe8a0abf0c5b73cec72ae1d8e5eeba2882dc3c",
        "source": "derived"
      },
      {
        "position": 10,
        "text": "SCOPE EXCLUSIONS. Do not add a public preparation family; own task-directed state or recovery (WK-2437); own atomic mutation (WK-2438); own workflow reporting (WK-2055); alter proof-pack semantics; infer proof applicability; add policy/admission authority; implement stale rebase (WK-2427); change query cursor semantics (WK-2436); or duplicate generic proof-plan skeleton work delivered by WK-2024.",
        "identity": "derived:5485728656f73a37a61bb6c7571385a87bc8b450d20e5aa01415e6915ea91bbc",
        "source": "derived"
      }
    ],
